{#
  T-5.01 — the sign-in sheet.

  WHAT THIS COMPONENT IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. `SignIn Bottom Sheet Step 1.pdf`
  draws a bottom sheet titled «تسجيل الدخول» with a ✕, a rule reading «اختر
  الوسيلة المناسبة», and a two-way choice between «رسالة نصية» and «البريد
  الإلكتروني». **The sheet is this theme's. The choice inside it is not, and
  cannot be.**

  `salla-login-modal`'s entire `render()` is an `<iframe>` pointing at
  `accounts.salla.com`, and its `postMessage` bridge validates that origin
  strictly. The method choice, the identifier field and the verification code are
  Salla's own pages on Salla's own origin. **No CSS crosses that boundary and no
  subclass reaches inside it** — so the backlog's «technique C preferred, B if
  presentation cannot be overridden» was not available in either form. Read in
  the component's source, not assumed.

  **The project owner ruled on 2026-08-10** that the platform's flow is kept and
  re-presented in this theme's shell rather than rebuilt on `salla.auth.api`.
  That keeps passkeys, guest checkout and new-customer registration working — all
  three live inside that iframe, and none of them is drawn by any artboard. The
  cost is that the segmented choice does not look like the artboard, and it is
  recorded as AC-9 in `/docs/DERIVED-DECISIONS.md` rather than left to be
  discovered.

  WHY `inline`. Without it the component renders its own `<salla-modal>`, which
  is the wrong shape (centred, not bottom-anchored) and carries the four
  accessibility defects T-2.10 exists to avoid — no focus trap, no Esc, no focus
  return, no initial focus on a sheet made of buttons. With it, `render()` returns
  the iframe alone and this file supplies the shell: T-2.10's `<dialog>`, which
  gets all four from `showModal()`.

  The component still drives its own visibility through `this.modal`, which the
  inline branch never assigns — `partials/auth.js` supplies it, and the reason
  that is the platform's own idiom rather than a hack is written there.
#}
{% set login_body %}
    {#
      The iframe is created by the component only once `login::open` has fired,
      so this container is empty on first paint. It carries the reserved height
      rather than the iframe: the height arrives later, over `postMessage`, and a
      sheet that opened at zero and jumped to full size would be the CLS this
      theme forbids.
    #}
    <div class="login-sheet__frame">
        <salla-login-modal inline data-testid="store-login-modal"></salla-login-modal>
    </div>
{% endset %}

{% include 'components.ui.bottom-sheet' with {
    id:    'login-sheet',
    title: trans('theme.auth.title'),
    body:  login_body,
    class: 'sheet--login'
} %}
